      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَيْتٌ مُسَجَّفٌ</span></b>  [<i>A tent;</i> or <i>chamber,</i>] <i>having a
pair of curtains</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِجْفَانِ</span>) <i>upon its entrance,</i> or
<i>door.</i> (As, TA.) El-Farezdak applies this masc.
sing. epithet to a pl. n., saying <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحِجَالُ المُسَجَّفُ</span>.
(TA.)

